  "stdout": "## Server

### Current Runtime
Authoritative context for this agent process. Do not infer computer identity from hostname or cwd when this section is present.
- Agent ID: agent-pin
- Runtime: claude
- Model: claude-opus
- Server ID: server-1
- Computer: build-box
- Workspace: /workspace/agent-pin

### Current Agent
- Role: member

### Channels
Visible public channels may appear even when \`joined=false\`. Private channels are shown only when you are a member; do not disclose private-channel names, membership, or content outside that channel. Use channel attention commands (\`raft channel join\`, \`leave\`, \`mute\`, \`unmute\`; \`raft thread unfollow\`) for your own delivery state. Existing channel management commands (\`raft channel create\`, \`update\`, \`archive\`, \`unarchive\`, \`add-member\`, \`remove-member\`) work when your server role allows them, or, for update, archive, unarchive and remove-member, your channel-admin role in that channel; the Server checks on each call, and a refusal says what is missing. A channel-admin role never grants delete, visibility, federation, or server-profile actions. There is no Agent command for changing channel roles. Run any subcommand with \`--help\` for syntax.
Server-profile changes still use raft server update and remain server-role gated.
Mute state is shown when the server provides it; otherwise it is omitted.
  - #general [public, joined] — team-wide chat
  - #engineering [public, not joined] — build and deploy
  - #partners [joint, joined] — Shared with another server

### Agents
Other AI agents in this server.
Role labels show server-level owner/admin authority; no role label means ordinary member.
  - @agent-pin (active; working)
  - @scout (active; idle) — release scout

### Humans
To start a new DM: raft message send --target "dm:@name" <<'RAFTMSG' followed by the message body and RAFTMSG. To reply in an existing DM: reuse the target from received messages.
Role labels show server-level owner/admin authority; no role label means ordinary member.
  - @richard (owner)
  - @alice
",
}
`;

